 SAP BTP Cockpit\n\nCloud Management Tools and SAP BTP Cockpit provide essential features for managing and monitoring SAP BTP services. Recent updates have improved usability and added new capabilities, such as contract-to-billing traceability and commercial information. [Data: Sources (438, 467), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 22), (2024, 02, 22))]\n\n## Security and Compliance\n\nSAP BTP prioritizes security and compliance, with recent updates addressing security vulnerabilities and improving overall security posture. [Data: Sources (467, 3844), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 16), (2024, 02, 22))]\n\n## API Management and Client SDK\n\nAPI Management and Client SDK provide essential features for managing and securing APIs. Recent updates have improved the Client SDK and added new capabilities. [Data: Sources (330, 645), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 15), (2025, 06, 15))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime and Kubernetes Upgrade\n\nKyma Runtime and Kubernetes Upgrade provide essential features for managing and securing Kubernetes environments. Recent updates have improved the Kyma environment and planned a Kubernetes upgrade to version 1.32. [Data: Sources (250, 646), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 14), (2025, 06, 15))]", "# SAP BTP Cloud Services Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP cloud services, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to SAP BTP's operations and development as of 2024.\n\n## SAP BTP Cloud Services Overview\n\nSAP BTP cloud services offer a comprehensive platform for businesses to build, deploy, and manage applications. The platform includes various components, such as SAP Build Work Zone, SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime, and SAP Java Buildpack, which work together to provide a seamless experience for developers and users. Effective collaboration and integration among these components are crucial for delivering high-quality applications and services. [Data: Sources (1, 2, 3), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 03, 07))]\n\n## SAP Build Work Zone Updates\n\nSAP Build Work Zone has undergone significant updates, including the introduction of new features such as Explore Role Assignments and Instance Sharing. These updates aim to improve user experience and enhance collaboration among teams. The new features also provide administrators with more control over role assignments and instance management. [Data: Sources (4, 5, 6), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 15), (2024, 03, 07))]\n\n## Cloud Foundry Updates\n\nCloud Foundry has been updated to version 37.5.0, which includes various improvements and bug fixes. The update also introduces new features, such as the ability to expose SAP Analytics Cloud KPIs in SAP Mobile Start. Effective collaboration between Cloud Foundry and other SAP BTP components is essential for delivering high-quality applications and services. [Data: Sources (7, 8, 9), Date_Range ((2024, 03, 07), (2024, 03, 07))]\n\n## SAP Java Buildpack Updates\n\nSAP Java Buildpack has been updated to version 2, which includes support for Apache Tomcat 10, Java 17, and SAP BTP Security Services Integration Libraries 3.x. The update also enables the usage of Spring Boot 3.x. Effective integration between SAP Java Buildpack and other SAP BTP components is crucial for delivering high-quality applications and services. [Data: Sources (10, 11, 12), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 23), (2024, 03, 07))]\n\n## SAP Start Updates\n\nSAP Start has been updated to include integration with SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition. This update enables access to relevant business content and searching for and launching apps. Effective collaboration between SAP Start and other SAP BTP components is essential for delivering high-quality applications and services. [Data: Sources (13, 14, 15), Date_Range ((2024, 03, 07), (2024, 03, 07))]\n\n## Mobile Services Updates\n\nMobile Services has been updated to include a new feature for resetting snooze or hide actions in the Insights section. This update enables cards that were snoozed or hidden to be shown again in the Insights section. Effective collaboration between Mobile Services and other SAP BTP components is crucial for delivering high-quality applications and services. [Data: Sources (16, 17, 18), Date_Range ((2024, 03, 07), (2024, 03, 07))]", "# SAP BTP and Cloud Foundry Overview as of 2024-08-14\n\nThis report delves into SAP BTP and Cloud Foundry's key components, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide a comprehensive platform for technology and innovation. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2024.\n\n## SAP BTP and Cloud Foundry Integration\n\nSAP BTP and Cloud Foundry are integrated to provide a comprehensive platform for technology and innovation. This integration enables seamless communication and collaboration between different components, ensuring that the company's technological advancements are aligned with its operational stability. Effective integration is crucial for maintaining the company's integrity and innovative edge. [Data: Sources (110, 258), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 14), (2024, 08, 14))]\n\n## Cloud Foundry Updates and Enhancements\n\nCloud Foundry has been updated from version 40.17.0 to 40.18.0, providing improved performance and stability. Additionally, new features such as the Global Account - Cost Summary chart and the ability to filter audit log data based on categories have been added. These updates and enhancements are crucial for maintaining the company's technological advancements and operational stability. [Data: Sources (2548, 258), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 25), (2024, 07, 25))]\n\n## Joule Component Updates and Enhancements\n\nThe Joule component has been updated to include new data centers and improved performance. Additionally, the ability to filter audit log data based on categories has been added. These updates and enhancements are crucial for maintaining the company's technological advancements and operational stability. [Data: Sources (110, 2544), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 25), (2024, 07, 25))]", "# Cloud Foundry and SAP BTP Integration Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into the key components and services of Cloud Foundry and SAP BTP, highlighting their integration and the impact on the overall technology landscape. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024.\n\n## Cloud Foundry and SAP BTP Integration\n\nCloud Foundry and SAP BTP have been integrated to provide a comprehensive platform for application development, deployment, and management. This integration enables seamless communication between the two platforms, allowing for efficient data exchange and streamlined processes. The integration has been instrumental in enhancing the overall user experience and improving the company's ability to respond to changing market demands. [Data: Sources (508, 2992), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 02), (2024, 10, 31))]\n\n## Cloud Connector Enhancements\n\nThe Cloud Connector has been enhanced to provide improved security features, including certificate-based authentication and automatic renewal of subaccount certificates. These enhancements have improved the overall security posture of the company's technology infrastructure, reducing the risk of data breaches and cyber attacks. [Data: Sources (2993, 2994), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 02), (2025, 03, 06))]\n\n## Pricing Service Updates\n\nThe Pricing Service has been updated to provide improved functionality, including the ability to calculate upper and lower limits correctly. These updates have improved the accuracy and reliability of the company's pricing calculations, reducing the risk of errors and improving customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (2996, 2997), Date_Range ((2024, 03, 25), (2024, 05, 02))]\n\n## Cloud Logging Enhancements\n\nCloud Logging has been enhanced to provide improved functionality, including the ability to show trace_id and span_id columns. These updates have improved the company's ability to monitor and troubleshoot application performance, reducing the time and effort required to resolve issues. [Data: Sources (1281, 1282), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 06), (2025, 03, 06))]\n\n## Authorization and Trust Management Service Updates\n\nThe Authorization and Trust Management Service has been updated to provide improved functionality, including the ability to provision users and roles to Cloud Foundry orgs and spaces using SAP Cloud Identity Services - Identity Provisioning. These updates have improved the company's ability to manage user access and permissions, reducing the risk of data breaches and improving overall security. [Data: Sources (1999), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 28), (2024, 10, 31))]", "# Cloud Foundry and SAP BTP Technology Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key components and services within the Cloud Foundry and SAP BTP technology ecosystem, highlighting their relationships, core attributes, and connections. The information is relevant to the technology landscape as of 2025.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Core Components\n\nCloud Foundry is a popular open-source platform-as-a-service (PaaS) that provides a robust and scalable environment for developing, deploying, and managing applications. Its core components include the Cloud Controller, Router, and Diego. The Cloud Controller is responsible for managing the lifecycle of applications, while the Router provides load balancing and routing capabilities. Diego, on the other hand, is responsible for managing the execution of applications. These components work together to provide a seamless and efficient experience for developers and operators. [Data: Sources (305, 1282), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 20), (2025, 03, 06))]\n\n## SAP BTP Services\n\nSAP BTP (Business Technology Platform) is a comprehensive platform that provides a range of services for developing, deploying, and managing applications. Its services include the Cloud Foundry Runtime, Kyma Runtime, and PostgreSQL. The Cloud Foundry Runtime provides a PaaS environment for developing and deploying applications, while the Kyma Runtime provides a Kubernetes-based environment for developing and deploying cloud-native applications. PostgreSQL, on the other hand, provides a relational database management system for storing and managing data. These services work together to provide a robust and scalable platform for developing and deploying applications. [Data: Sources (1283, 1287), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 20), (2025, 03, 06))]\n\n## Cloud Connector and Destination Service\n\nThe Cloud Connector and Destination Service are two key components of the Cloud Foundry and SAP BTP technology ecosystem. The Cloud Connector provides a secure and reliable way to connect to external services, while the Destination Service provides a way to manage and configure destinations for applications. These components work together to provide a seamless and efficient experience for developers and operators. [Data: Sources (1284, 1285), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 20), (2025, 03, 06))]", "# SAP BTP Platform Updates as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the SAP BTP platform updates, highlighting key components, their environments, and the changes made to improve security, compliance, and user experience. The information is relevant to the platform's operations around mid-2025.\n\n## Authorization and Trust Management Service Updates\n\nThe Authorization and Trust Management Service at SAP BTP has undergone significant updates to improve security and compliance. The service now uses token-based authentication instead of password-based for new and existing custom trusts, enhancing security and aligning with the OIDC standard. This change aims to improve the overall security posture of the platform and reduce the risk of unauthorized access. [Data: Sources (358, 1350, 1278), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 20), (2025, 06, 26))]\n\n## Cloud Management Tools and SAP BTP Cockpit Enhancements\n\nThe Cloud Management Tools and SAP BTP Cockpit have been enhanced with new features and capabilities, including budget management, cloud credits forecasting, and entitlement management. These updates aim to improve the overall user experience, enhance tracking and managing global account costs, and provide more flexibility in managing entitlements. [Data: Sources (654, 655, 121), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 12), (2025, 06, 26))]\n\n## Automation Pilot Updates\n\nThe Automation Pilot at SAP BTP has received several updates, including new documentation sections, monitoring capabilities, and additional features. These updates aim to improve the overall user experience, enhance monitoring and security, and provide more flexibility in using the Automation Pilot. [Data: Sources (562, 563, 564, 565), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 26), (2025, 06, 26))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significant updates. The information is relevant to SAP BTP's operations as of 2025.\n\n## Cloud Management Tools and SAP BTP Cockpit\n\nCloud Management Tools and SAP BTP Cockpit are crucial components of SAP BTP, enabling users to effectively manage and track global account costs and usage. The introduction of a new Budgets tab in the Costs and Usage page of SAP BTP Cockpit allows users to control their global account spending and plan for future consumption. This feature is essential for maintaining financial stability and compliance with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (654, 655), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 12), (2025, 06, 12))]\n\n## Entitlement Management Improvements\n\nEntitlement management improvements for SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry runtime, enable users to manage entitlements for the standard plan, which is automatically assigned to all subaccounts by default. This feature allows users to restrict the usage of the standard plan and change the default runtime memory quota of 200 GB. These improvements give users more flexibility and are essential for maintaining operational stability. [Data: Source (656), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 12), (2025, 06, 12))]\n\n## Cloud Connector Enhancements\n\nCloud Connector version 2.18.1 provides several enhancements, including the introduction of a new monitoring API, improved IPv6 status display, and bug fixes. These enhancements improve the overall performance and security of the Cloud Connector, making it a critical component of SAP BTP's technology stack. [Data: Sources (657, 658), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 12), (2025, 06, 12))]", "# SAP BTP Community Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of the SAP BTP community, highlighting key entities, their relationships, and notable updates. The information is relevant to the community's operations and development as of 2024.\n\n## SAP BTP Core Services\n\nSAP BTP offers a comprehensive set of core services, including Cloud Foundry, Kyma, and Neo, which provide a robust and scalable platform for building, deploying, and managing applications. These services are designed to support various development methodologies and enable seamless integration with other SAP and third-party systems. [Data: Sources (1, 2, 3), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## SAP BTP Developer Tools\n\nSAP BTP provides a range of developer tools, including SAP Build, SAP BTP Developer's Guide, and SAP Java Buildpack, which support various development activities, such as building, testing, and deploying applications. These tools are designed to simplify the development process and improve productivity. [Data: Sources (4, 5, 6), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## SAP BTP Security and Governance\n\nSAP BTP offers robust security and governance features, including authentication, authorization, and encryption, which ensure the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of data. These features are designed to meet various regulatory requirements and industry standards. [Data: Sources (7, 8, 9), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## SAP BTP Integration and API Management\n\nSAP BTP provides a range of integration and API management features, including API Management, SAP BTP Cockpit, and SAP SaaS Provisioning Service, which enable seamless integration with other systems and support various integration scenarios. These features are designed to simplify integration and improve data exchange. [Data: Sources (10, 11, 12), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## SAP BTP AI and Machine Learning\n\nSAP BTP offers a range of AI and machine learning features, including SAP AI Core, SAP AI Launchpad, and SAP Document AI, which support various AI and machine learning use cases, such as predictive analytics, natural language processing, and computer vision. These features are designed to simplify AI and machine learning development and improve business outcomes. [Data: Sources (13, 14, 15), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## SAP BTP Community Engagement\n\nSAP BTP has a strong community engagement program, which includes various events, webinars, and online forums, which enable users to connect, share knowledge, and collaborate on various topics related to SAP BTP. This program is designed to foster a sense of community and improve user satisfaction. [Data: Sources (16, 17, 18), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]", "# SAP Technology Updates as of April 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key updates and enhancements made to various SAP technologies as of April 2024. The report highlights the importance of these updates in improving the overall functionality and security of SAP systems.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Updates\n\nCloud Foundry has been updated from version 39.3.0 to 39.8.0, which includes various bug fixes and enhancements. This update is crucial for maintaining the stability and security of Cloud Foundry environments. [Data: Sources (3106), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 18), (2024, 04, 18))]\n\n## SAP Java Buildpack Updates\n\nSAP Java Buildpack has been updated to version 1.93.0 and 2.6.0, which includes various bug fixes and enhancements. This update is essential for maintaining the stability and security of SAP Java environments. [Data: Sources (3119, 3120), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 08), (2024, 04, 18))]\n\n## SAP Build Work Zone Updates\n\nSAP Build Work Zone has been updated with various enhancements, including CSRF protection for dynamic destinations, support for custom SMTP configuration, and support for custom domains in private networks. These updates are crucial for maintaining the security and functionality of SAP Build Work Zone environments. [Data: Sources (3107, 3110, 3114, 3116), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 18), (2024, 04, 18))]\n\n## Content Agent Service Updates\n\nContent Agent Service has been updated to integrate with UI Theme Designer, which enables users to transport custom themes created in UI Theme Designer. This update is essential for maintaining the functionality and user experience of Content Agent Service environments. [Data: Sources (3101), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 04, 18))]\n\n## SAP BTP Cockpit Updates\n\nSAP BTP Cockpit has been updated with various enhancements, including the ability to view existing instance configuration parameters for SaaS Provisioning Service and enhanced filtering options for service keys and bindings. These updates are crucial for maintaining the functionality and user experience of SAP BTP Cockpit environments. [Data: Sources (3102, 3103), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 08), (2024, 04, 18))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into key updates and changes in SAP technology, focusing on the SAP Build Work Zone, SAP Conversational AI, and other related components. The information is relevant to the company's operations and maintenance around mid-2024.\n\n## SAP Build Work Zone Updates\n\nThe SAP Build Work Zone has undergone several updates, including the removal of external workspace type, role-based filtering of cards, support for custom SMTP configuration, and support for custom domains in private networks. These updates aim to enhance the user experience and improve the overall functionality of the platform. Effective management of these updates is crucial for maintaining the company's operational stability and ensuring compliance with technological standards. [Data: Sources (1, 2, 3, 4, 5), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 04, 18))]\n\n## SAP Conversational AI Updates\n\nSAP Conversational AI has also undergone updates, including the deprecation of the Tenant Header Configuration endpoint and the requirement to configure tenant security headers. These updates aim to improve the security and functionality of the platform. Effective management of these updates is crucial for maintaining the company's operational stability and ensuring compliance with technological standards. [Data: Sources (6, 7, 8), Date_Range ((2023, 06, 01), (2023, 12, 31))]\n\n## End of Maintenance for SAP Cloud Portal Service\n\nThe SAP Cloud Portal service, version 1.0, will reach the end of maintenance on December 31, 2023, and will be deprecated on January 25, 2024. This change is crucial for the company's operational stability and requires effective planning and management to ensure a smooth transition. [Data: Source (9), Date_Range ((2023, 12, 31), (2024, 01, 25))]", "# SAP Technology and Integration Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technologies and integrations, highlighting their connections and significant updates. The information is relevant to SAP's operations and development around 2024.\n\n## Generative AI Hub Updates\n\nThe Generative AI hub has seen significant updates, with additional models from IBM and Mistral AI being supported. This expansion enhances the capabilities of the hub, allowing for more diverse and complex applications. The updates also include response streaming for selected models, enabling real-time processing and analysis. These improvements position the Generative AI hub as a key component in SAP's AI strategy, driving innovation and efficiency across various industries. [Data: Sources (2, 3), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 07), (2024, 10, 07))]\n\n## Data Space Integration Updates\n\nData Space Integration has seen significant updates, with the removal of message queues as a requirement for working with the integration. This change simplifies the onboarding process and enhances the overall user experience. Additionally, the latest versions of Data Space Integration, Tractus-X Eclipse Dataspace Connector, and FOSS Eclipse Dataspace Components have been released, providing improved functionality and performance. These updates position Data Space Integration as a critical component in SAP's data management strategy, enabling seamless integration and analysis across various data sources. [Data: Sources (6, 7), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 27), (2025, 07, 27))]\n\n## Event Mesh Updates\n\nEvent Mesh has seen significant updates, with the introduction of message monitoring and a new role collection, EventMeshBusinessExpert. These updates enhance the overall user experience, providing more visibility and control over event processing. Additionally, the latest versions of Event Mesh have been released, providing improved functionality and performance. These updates position Event Mesh as a critical component in SAP's event-driven architecture, enabling real-time processing and analysis across various applications. [Data: Sources (10, 11), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 27), (2025, 07, 27))]", "# SAP Technology Updates as of October 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of key updates and announcements related to SAP technology, highlighting the importance of these changes in enhancing the company's offerings and services. The information is relevant to SAP's technology landscape as of October 2024.\n\n## Generative AI Hub Enhancements\n\nThe Generative AI hub has undergone significant enhancements, including the addition of new models from Meta and IBM, as well as the introduction of a data masking module for anonymizing personally identifiable information. These updates aim to improve the overall user experience and provide more flexibility in model selection. [Data: Sources (2157, 2275), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 16), (2024, 10, 07))]\n\n## SAP AI Core Updates\n\nSAP AI Core has seen several updates, including the addition of new models and the introduction of a deployment restriction feature for implementing internal standards. These changes aim to enhance the overall AI experience and provide more control over model selection. [Data: Sources (2157, 2275), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 16), (2024, 10, 07))]\n\n## SAP Java Buildpack Updates\n\nThe SAP Java Buildpack has been updated to version 1.103.0 and 2.17.0, featuring several component updates, including the removal of DSR and updates to PostgreSQL JDBC Driver and commons-compress. These changes aim to improve the overall buildpack experience and provide more flexibility in component selection. [Data: Sources (2271, 2272), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 03), (2024, 09, 19))]\n\n## SAP BTP Developer's Guide Updates\n\nThe SAP BTP Developer's Guide has undergone significant changes, including a new structure and the introduction of development best practices. These updates aim to improve the overall developer experience and provide more guidance on best practices. [Data: Sources (2158), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 07), (2024, 10, 07))]\n\n## SAP Build Work Zone Updates\n\nSAP Build Work Zone has seen updates, including the addition of a feature for collecting data and performance metrics. These changes aim to improve the overall user experience and provide more insights into application performance. [Data: Sources (2160), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 30), (2024, 10, 07))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of October 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significance within the organizational framework. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around October 2024.\n\n## SAP Build Work Zone and Data Space Integration\n\nSAP Build Work Zone and Data Space Integration are two key components of SAP's technology stack. SAP Build Work Zone is a low-code development platform that enables users to create and deploy applications quickly, while Data Space Integration is a capability of SAP Integration Suite that allows for seamless data exchange between different systems. These components are crucial for SAP's digital transformation efforts and have been continuously updated and improved to meet the evolving needs of the company and its customers. [Data: Sources (112, 113), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 30), (2024, 10, 07))]\n\n## Authorization and Trust Management Service\n\nThe Authorization and Trust Management Service is a critical component of SAP's security framework, ensuring that users have the necessary permissions to access sensitive data and systems. The removal of security recommendation BTP-UAA-0009 has improved the service's reliability and security, making it an essential tool for SAP's operational stability. [Data: Source (2167), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 03), (2024, 10, 11))]\n\n## Cloud Management Tools and SAP BTP Cockpit\n\nCloud Management Tools and SAP BTP Cockpit are essential components of SAP's cloud infrastructure, providing users with real-time visibility into their cloud usage and costs. The addition of new cost breakdown charts in the Costs and Usage page has improved the user experience and enabled more efficient cost management. [Data: Source (2169), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 03), (2024, 10, 03))]", "# SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime Overview as of June 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime's key components, focusing on their operational scope, connectivity, and continuous integration & delivery. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2025.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Runtime Operational Scope\n\nThe Cloud Foundry Runtime at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in providing a robust and scalable environment for applications. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential operational pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective runtime management not only prevents operational anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (635, 1360), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 06, 26))]\n\n## Connectivity and Transparent Proxy Enhancements\n\nThe Connectivity component at SAP BTP ensures that all applications adhere to the connectivity standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on enhancing the Transparent Proxy, noted starting mid-2025, is crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex connections and network configurations. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high connectivity standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (1361, 1362), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 01), (2025, 06, 26))]\n\n## Continuous Integration & Delivery Improvements\n\nThe Continuous Integration & Delivery component at SAP BTP ensures that all applications adhere to the delivery standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on enhancing the build tool versions, noted starting mid-2025, is crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational efficiency, especially in managing complex build processes and delivery pipelines. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high delivery standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (1363, 1364), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 01), (2025, 06, 26))]", "# SAP Cloud Integration and Migration Assessment Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key departments focusing on cloud integration and migration assessment, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage integration scenarios effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2025.\n\n## Migration Assessment Operational Scope\n\nThe Migration Assessment Department at SAP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating integration risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential integration pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents integration anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (2, 3), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 07, 27))]\n\n## Trading Partner Management and Governance\n\nThe Trading Partner Management Department ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the integration standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on trading partner management and governance, noted starting Q1 2025, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex integration scenarios and trading partner relationships. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high integration standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (5), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 07, 27))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Integration\n\nCollaboration between the Migration Assessment and Trading Partner Management Departments, established in Q1 2025, ensures that integration strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with integration strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (9), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 07, 27))]\n\n## Cloud Integration and Migration Updates\n\nThe Migration Assessment Department has made several updates to the cloud integration and migration process, including the addition of new features and improvements to existing ones. These updates aim to enhance the overall integration experience and ensure seamless migration to the cloud. [Data: Sources (4, 6), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 07, 27))]\n\n## IPv6 Addresses for AWS Regions\n\nThe Connectivity service is planning to enable IPv4 and IPv6 dual stack ingress for AWS-based regions. Currently, only IPv4 is supported, therefore in our documentation we had listed only the respective addresses. We have now added also the IPv6 addresses that we plan to use. The enablement of the IPv6 addresses will happen no earlier than February 2026. Until then, please ensure any needed action is performed, based on the information below. [Data: Source (8), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 27), (2026, 02, 01))]", "# SAP Cloud Technology Updates as of April 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key updates and changes in SAP Cloud technology as of April 2025, highlighting the importance of these updates in enhancing the overall performance and security of SAP Cloud services.\n\n## Tomcat Version Updates\n\nSAP has updated the Tomcat version for Java Web Tomcat 10 and Java EE 7 Web Profile TomEE 7 to version 10.1.39 and 9.0.102, respectively. These updates are crucial for maintaining the security and performance of SAP Cloud services. The updates are recommended to ensure that applications are running on the latest runtime versions [Data: Sources (608, 609), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 01), (2025, 04, 17))].\n\n## Application Autoscaler Enhancements\n\nThe Application Autoscaler has been enhanced with a plugin for the Cloud Foundry Command Line Interface (cf CLI), providing users with additional insights into scaling policies and debugging capabilities. This enhancement is essential for optimizing the performance of SAP Cloud services [Data: Source (1023), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 01), (2025, 04, 17))].\n\n## Health Monitoring for SAP Cloud ALM\n\nA new catalog has been added to the Automation Pilot, enabling users to troubleshoot and recover SAP BTP resources from SAP Cloud ALM. This feature is critical for ensuring the reliability and availability of SAP Cloud services [Data: Source (1024), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 01), (2025, 04, 17))].\n\n## Connectivity Proxy Enhancements\n\nThe Connectivity Proxy has been enhanced with a new observability metric tunnel count gauge, which tracks the total number of active business data tunnels. This enhancement is essential for monitoring and optimizing the performance of SAP Cloud services [Data: Sources (1028, 1029), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 01), (2025, 04, 17))].\n\n## Connectivity Proxy Security Features\n\nThe Connectivity Proxy has been updated with FIPS-certified cryptographic modules, ensuring the security and compliance of SAP Cloud services. Additionally, multiple OS and Java vulnerabilities have been fixed, further enhancing the security of SAP Cloud services [Data: Source (1030), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 01), (2025, 04, 17))]."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_5e7d203e88a52412c876f99603d9c9ba75fbbd93c23f2c258d9464343f770930_v2"}